   292	    - Exactly one green (3) cell lies on a border and marks the route's start.
   293	
   294	    Rule:
   295	    - Each bar forbids all cells within Manhattan distance <= (bar_length - blue_count), i.e. its red-cell count.
   296	    - Among all cells that avoid every bar halo, draw the shortest axis-aligned path from the green start to the opposite edge using BFS.
   297	    - After the path is painted, recolor every blue bar cell to red.
   298	
